  "scope": "Phase-three Building Blocks browser: workspace instances, versioned catalog projection, owned multi-block drag data, help bindings, default docking and ordered focus requests. No SDK or viewport transfer changes.",
  "status": "Building Blocks migration is complete. Data Resources and default contribution configuration remain in phase three; completed_phase stays 2.",
  "implemented": [
    "Building Blocks is a registered view type. Filter, category, selection, expansion and sorting belong to each instance; state has a version and contains prototype GUIDs rather than native catalog indices.",
    "catalog.building-blocks exposes bounded, versioned pages of copied UTF-8 data. Published metadata remains readable during native work. Native catalog changes invalidate view projections without per-frame native queries.",
    "Removed BuildingBlocksPanel and its private fields from EditorPanels. The primary browser uses a pinned workspace role; extra instances use the same creation, navigation, focus, inspection and closure as independent modules.",
    "ImGui owns the complete ordered drag list and source row. Schematic, Layout and scene trees decode the same bounded data. Insertion preserves catalog order; replacement keeps the actual dragged prototype. Removed global draggedBlocks from EditorState.",
    "HTML help uses the registered help.open command. Drawing consumes the actual configured chord, preventing the global action from reopening the default topic after a remapped key.",
    "Workspace docks all registered instances by type and closes separated views before removing old dock nodes. Multiple pending focus requests retain the last requested focus independently of instance/drawing order, including provider replacement.",
    "Browsing does not mark a document interaction active; focused resource windows cannot reject a prepared document switch. Public C/C++ headers expose no SDK or STL types."
  ],
